        <mxCell id="1FbOqA_suXgTDa79VxNz-7" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;fontColor=#000000;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#FFF9B2;strokeColor=none;fillStyle=solid;direction=west;gradientDirection=north;gradientColor=#FFF2A1;shadow=1;size=20;pointerEvents=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;Function calling is a feature of LLMs, where LLMs determines if external functions must be called and with what parameters, so that the application/ agent/ Semantic Kernel calls the function. The LLM uses the function response to generate its own response.&lt;br&gt;The&lt;br/&gt;LLM does not call the function directly. Instead, the client application does.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;In&lt;br&gt;function calling, the LLM asks the client application to call external&lt;br&gt;functions." vertex="1">
